award to a woman who resigns within three months of delivery | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` `[BOE — official English]` |
| Arts. 155 (M/134), 156 (repealed), 157 | The employer may not dismiss a female worker, or warn her of dismissal, during her pregnancy or maternity leave, including any period of illness resulting from either, proven by an approved medical certificate, provided her absence does not exceed 180 days a year, continuous or intermittent (Art. 155). Art. 156 was repealed by M/134. A female worker forfeits her entitlements under this Part if she works for another employer during her authorised leave, and the original employer may withhold or recover her leave pay (Art. 157) | لا يجوز لصاحب العمل فصل العاملة أو إنذارها بالفصل أثناء حملها أو تمتعها بإجازة الوضع، ويشمل ذلك مدة مرضها الناشئ عن أي منهما، على أن يثبت المرض بشهادة طبية معتمدة، وأن لا تتجاوز مدة غيابها (مائة وثمانين) يوماً في السنة | Protected period covers the entire pregnancy (from its start, not from notification) through maternity leave and related illness up to 180 days' absence a year; a dismissal notice served in that window is itself prohibited. The 2005 text's separate 180-day pre-delivery protection (old Art. 156) is repealed and folded into Art. 155. Termination for an Art. 80 ground during pregnancy is not expressly excepted; treat as high risk `[model knowledge — verify]` | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` `[BOE — official English]` |
