# Implementing Regulations of the Labor Law and its Annexes — اللائحة التنفيذية لنظام العمل وملحقاتها

<!-- Written 2026-09-04 from the HRSD April-2025 consolidated Arabic PDF (authority/hrsd-labor-regs-2025-04-ar.txt), the HRSD 2023 English translation of the pre-amendment regulations (authority/hrsd-labor-regs-2023-en.txt), the HRSD page for Ministerial Decision 115921, and the Labor Law Arabic text on laws.boe.gov.sa (boe/labor-law-ar.md, regenerated 2026-09-04 so that each amended article is marked [معدلة] and carries the amending blocks after the original text). -->

## Instrument

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Jurisdiction | `ksa` |
| Instrument | Implementing Regulations of the Labor Law and its Annexes (Annex 1 unified model work regulations; Annex 2 accommodations for workers with disabilities; Annex 3 rules for the activity of intermediation in employing Saudis; Annex 4 rules for the recruitment and labor-services activity; Annex 5 unified model employment contracts) / اللائحة التنفيذية لنظام العمل وملحقاتها (الملحق 1 النموذج الموحد للائحة تنظيم العمل؛ الملحق 2 جدول الترتيبات والخدمات التيسيرية؛ الملحق 3 ضوابط التوسط في توظيف السعوديين؛ الملحق 4 قواعد ممارسة نشاط الاستقدام وتقديم الخدمات العمالية؛ الملحق 5 النماذج الموحدة لعقد العمل بأنواعه) |
| Issuing instrument | Ministerial Decision No. 115921 of 19/8/1446H (the number 115921 and the date 1446/08/19 are legible in the OCR of `authority/hrsd-decision-115921-ar.txt`; the HRSD page for the decision states that it approves the Regulations "to replace the Implementing Regulations issued by Ministerial Decision No. 70273 of 11/4/1440H and its amendments"). The operative paragraphs of the decision itself are not legible in the OCR and were not read. |
| Issuing authority | Ministry of Human Resources and Social Development (HRSD) / وزارة الموارد البشرية والتنمية الاجتماعية |
| Effective date | 2025-02-19 (task brief). The Regulations implement the Labor Law amendments of Royal Decree M/44 of 8/2/1446H, which the BOE portal states apply from 20/8/1446H (= 19 February 2025). The decision's own commencement clause was not legible in the source and was not read `[model knowledge — verify]`. |
| Amendment history | Replaces the 1440H Regulations (Ministerial Decision 70273 of 11/4/1440H) and their later amendments (the 2023 English edition prints a decision that deleted para 3 of clause 7 of Art. 38 and re-worded paras 1 and 5 of clause 8 of Art. 38 — the 90-day settlement request and 60-day settlement compliance windows). In the April-2025 Arabic edition: Arts. 2, 36 and 37 are marked "(ملغاة)" (repealed); Arts. 4 bis, 15 bis, 16 bis (1), 16 bis (2) and 22 bis are new; Art. 14 Second gains item 21 (transfer without consent after 12 months on 90 days' notice); Art. 19 (probation) and Art. 4 (approval route) are re-written; Art. 27 gains a "Second" part on flexible work (العمل المرن). No amendment of the 2025 edition itself was found in the files provided. |
| Official source (authoritative language) | https://www.hrsd.gov.sa/node/838894 (page title "اللائحة التنفيذية لنظام العمل وملحقاتها", carrying "قرار اعتماد اللائحة التنفيذية لنظام العمل وملحقاتها رقم 115921"; PDF read: `authority/hrsd-labor-regs-2025-04-ar.pdf`). Labor Law: https://laws.boe.gov.sa/BoeLaws/Laws/LawDetails/08381293-6388-48e2-8ad2-a9a700f2aa94/1 |
| Official translation | HRSD English translation of the 1440H Regulations as amended to 2023 (`authority/hrsd-labor-regs-2023-en.pdf`) — pre-dates Decision 115921; used only for English wording, mismatches flagged in the rows. No HRSD English of the 2025 edition was provided. Labor Law: Bureau of Experts official English (`labor-en.txt`, appendix includes M/44 of 1446H). |
| Text last read from the official source | 2026-09-04 (Arabic 2025 PDF text; HRSD page last-modified stamp 2026-09-03; BOE Labor Law text with its [معدلة] amending blocks) |
| Post-cutoff amendment check | 2026-09-04: the HRSD page for Decision 115921 still presents it as the current Regulations and lists, as related items, a revised "جدول المخالفات والعقوبات لنظام العمل ولائحته التنفيذية", a "لائحة فحوصات اللياقة المهنية والأمراض غير المعدية" (Ministerial Decision 33232 of 11/3/1447H), and a project-management Saudization decision (70% from 14 February 2027). Their texts were not provided and were not read. `docs/amendment-watch-2026-09-04.md` lead 1.5 (penalties schedule revised effective 25 Feb 2026) and lead 1.1 (wage-clause direct enforcement phase 3 from 6 Aug 2026) are unverified. BOE Labor Law portal: issue date 23/8/1426H, publication 25/9/1426H, status "ساري", 106 articles marked as amended; amending instruments named on the portal: M/24 of 12/5/1434H, M/1 of 22/1/1435H (repeals Part XIV), M/46 of 5/6/1436H, M/14 of 22/2/1440H, M/134 of 27/11/1440H, M/5 of 7/1/1442H, M/44 of 8/2/1446H. In `boe/labor-law-ar.md` an amended article is headed "[معدلة]", its body is the original 2005 text under "النص الأصلي (قبل التعديل)", and the "تعديلات المادة" blocks that follow carry the wording in force; the amended wording was read from those blocks (107 headed articles counted today) and cross-checked against the portal HTML. Every Law row below states which version was read. |

## Scope

The Regulations execute the Labor Law article by article (each regulation article opens with "في تنفيذ أحكام المادة ... من النظام") and attach five annexes that are themselves binding templates: the unified work regulations that every establishment must adopt or adapt (Annex 1), the accommodations schedule for workers with disabilities (Annex 2), the licensing rules for placement of Saudis (Annex 3) and for recruitment and labor-services companies (Annex 4), and the unified employment-contract forms that Qiwa generates (Annex 5). They cover casual/temporary contracts, work-regulation approval, records, Saudization and Nitaqat, restricted professions, recruitment and transfer of services, training, contract documentation, probation, relocation, overtime and compensatory leave, exempt categories, public holidays, unpaid and sick leave, part-time and flexible work, work-injury reporting, first-aid, remote sites, nursing breaks, minors, and the mechanics of imposing, contesting and settling HRSD fines.

They do not contain: the Wage Protection System rules (only referenced: Law Art. 90(2) as amended, Annex 1 Art. 15, Annex 5 cl. 9.1.2/11.1, Annex 4 Art. 63), the ministerial schedule of violations and penalties (referenced by Art. 38), the Nitaqat program rules (referenced throughout Art. 14), the friendly-settlement rules for labor disputes, the domestic-workers regulation, or the substantive end-of-service and termination rules, which remain in the Labor Law itself (Arts. 74–88). Where a row below states a Labor Law rule it is because the Regulations quote or depend on it.

## Rules

Tag rules: `[settled — last confirmed YYYY-MM-DD]` only where the primary text was read on that date; `[model knowledge — verify]` for anything else, including practical-effect commentary that goes beyond the article's words. "Reg. Art." = article of the Regulations; "Annex 1 Art." = article of the unified model work regulations; "Annex 5 cl." = clause of the unified permanent-contract form; "Law Art." = Labor Law article.

| Article | Rule (English) | Rule (authoritative language) | Practical effect | Tag |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Reg. Art. 1 (Law Art. 6) | A temporary or casual contract that the parties continue to perform for more than ninety days becomes a contract subject to all provisions of the Labor Law, regardless of the visa title or residence period of an expatriate. Labor courts hear disputes under casual, seasonal and temporary contracts. | إذا استمر الطرفان في عقد العمل المؤقت أو العرضي في العمل لمدة تجاوزت تسعين يوماً تحول إلى عقد عمل يخضع لجميع أحكام نظام العمل؛ وتختص المحاكم العمالية بالنظر في الخلافات. | A "temporary" hire kept past day 90 accrues annual leave, sick leave and end-of-service award from day one of the converted contract. hiring-review must count days from actual start, not from the visa. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Reg. Art. 2 | Repealed ("ملغاة"). | (ملغاة) | The 2023 English Art. 2 defined "agricultural workers, shepherds and the like" (Law Art. 7(1)(d)); that definition no longer sits here. Law Art. 7 as amended by M/44 now directs the Minister to issue separate regulations for those categories. Do not cite Reg. Art. 2. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Reg. Art. 3 (Law Art. 12(1)) | The unified model work regulations in Annex 1 are the approved model. | يُعتمد النموذج الموحد للائحة تنظيم العمل بالصيغة المرافقة لهذه اللائحة (الملحق رقم 1). | Annex 1 is the baseline every handbook is measured against; policy-drafting and handbook-updates should diff a client handbook against Annex 1 clause by clause. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Reg. Art. 4(1) (Law Arts. 12(2), 13(2)) | Establishments must prepare their own work regulations, which must be reviewed and certified by a law firm accredited on the Ministry's website; the firm confirms there is no conflict with the Law, Regulations, annexes and implementing decisions, then submits them to the competent Ministry body. Establishments with fewer than fifty workers may instead select the unified model electronically without any change or addition and obtain an electronic certificate. | على المنشآت أن تقوم بإعداد لائحة تنظيم عمل خاصة بها ويشترط مراجعتها وتصديقها من مكاتب المحاماة المعتمدة على الموقع الإلكتروني للوزارة ... ويجوز للمنشآت التي يقل عدد عمالتها عن خمسون عامل اختيار النموذج الموحد إلكترونياً دون إجراء أي تعديل. | The lawyer-certification route is now the default; the "adopt the model unchanged" shortcut is limited to sub-50-headcount establishments. The 2023 English Art. 4 offered both routes to everyone with no headcount threshold — that text is superseded. Any bespoke clause (bonus scheme, extra leave, disciplinary ladder) means the lawyer route. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Reg. Art. 4(2) | Establishments with previously approved work regulations need not re-adopt the model if all their articles are consistent with the Law, the Regulations, the model and implementing decisions; conflicting articles are deemed repealed and of no effect and must be amended through the two routes in para 1. | تستثنى المنشآت التي سبق لها اعتماد لائحة تنظيم عمل خاصة بها ... أما إذا تضمنت مواد تتعارض مع ذلك فتعتبر تلك المواد ملغاة ولا يعتد بها وعلى المنشأة تعديل تلك المواد. | Grandfathering is conditional: a pre-2025 handbook with a 90-day probation cap, 10-week maternity leave, or old notice periods has those clauses void by operation of this paragraph. handbook-updates should treat the 2025 changes (probation, maternity, notice, resignation, compensatory leave) as forced amendments. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Reg. Art. 4 bis (Law Art. 15) | Establishments must update their data on the Ministry's approved platform within ten days of any change of address or data. | يجب على المنشآت تحديث بياناتها عبر المنصة المعتمدة من الوزارة في حال أي تغيير في عنوانها أو بياناتها خلال فترة لا تتجاوز عشرة (10) أيام. | New in 2025. A registered-office move or manager change triggers a 10-day Qiwa update `[model knowledge — verify]` that the platform is Qiwa. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Reg. Art. 5 (Law Art. 17) | Records to be kept at the workplace, paper or electronic: (1) worker roster with profession, age, nationality, ID and work-permit numbers and dates; (2) wage sheet with receipt dates, deductions and reasons; (3) fines register; (4) attendance register; (5) Saudi training register; (6) medical-examination register where occupational disease is possible; (7) a personnel file per worker with a copy of the contract and documents. | يجب على صاحب العمل تضمين الكشوف والسجلات والملفات التي يحتفظ بها في مكان العمل - سواء أكانت ورقية أم إلكترونية - البيانات التالية: كشف أسماء العمال، كشف أجور العمال، سجل قيد الغرامات، سجل الحضور والانصراف، سجل تدريب السعوديين، سجل الفحص الطبي، ملف عمل لكل عامل. | These seven records are what an HRSD inspector asks for; wage-hour-qa and internal-investigation should request the attendance register and fines register as primary evidence. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Reg. Art. 6 (Law Art. 20) | The employer may not retain a non-Saudi worker's passport, residence permit (iqama) or medical-insurance card. | على صاحب العمل عدم الاحتفاظ بجواز سفر العامل غير السعودي أو إقامته أو بطاقة التأمين الطبي. | A "passport safekeeping" clause in a contract or handbook is void and is a scheduled violation `[model knowledge — verify]` as to the fine amount. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Reg. Art. 8 (Law Art. 26(2)) | Saudization percentages are set through Ministry programs (e.g. Nitaqat), monitored per activity, and the Ministry withholds all or some of its services from establishments that do not meet them; the programs are updated periodically. | تحدد نسب التوطين لدى المنشآت الواجب تحقيقها من خلال برامج تضعها الوزارة ... وحجب كل أو بعض خدمات الوزارة عن المنشآت التي لا تحقق نسبة التوطين المحددة؛ مثل برنامج (نطاقات). | The statutory 75% in Law Art. 26(2) is displaced in practice by Nitaqat bands; the sanction is service suspension (visas, transfers, work-permit renewals), not a fine. Nitaqat rules are not in this file. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Reg. Art. 9 (Law Art. 28) | Defines "person with a disability" (medical report or HRSD card), "accommodations" (Saudi Building Code Part 2 and Annex 2), and "ability to work"; disability is not by itself a ground to refuse hiring, promotion or training if the person meets the job requirements; no wage discrimination on the ground of disability; establishments keep and disclose accommodation data to inspectors; any worker with a non-disabling illness of up to 120 days may use accommodations; counting a worker as more than one under Nitaqat requires an HRSD card and role-disability fit. | لا يجوز أن تكون الإعاقة بذاتها سبباً في رفض توظيف الأشخاص ذوي الإعاقة أو ترقيتهم أو استفادتهم من برامج التدريب المهني إذا توافر شرط القدرة على العمل ... لا يجوز التمييز في الأجور بين العاملين على أساس الإعاقة. | Together with Law Art. 61(4) (as amended by M/44: no exclusion, favoritism or discrimination on race, color, gender, age, disability, marital status) this is the KSA anti-discrimination baseline for hiring-review and internal-investigation. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Reg. Art. 10 (Law Art. 30) and Annexes 3–4 | Placement of Saudis, recruitment of workers and assignment (إسناد) of workers may only be practised under a Ministry licence; licences are granted, renewed and revoked under Ministry controls (Annex 3 for Saudi placement, Annex 4 for recruitment and labor services). Annex 4 Art. 70 prohibits practising or advertising these activities without a licence and prohibits any person from dealing with unlicensed companies; Annex 4 Art. 63 lists licensee prohibitions including delaying workers' wages and failing the Ministry's minimum wage-protection level (item ط) and providing labor services without documenting them on the Ajeer platform (item ن). Law Art. 229 bis (M/44 1446H): fine SAR 200,000–500,000 for breach of Art. 30(1). | لا يجوز لأي شخص طبيعي أو اعتباري أن يمارس نشاط توظيف السعوديين أو نشاط استقدام العمال أو نشاط الإسناد ما لم يكن مرخصاً له بذلك من الوزارة ... يعاقب بغرامة لا تقل عن (200,000) ولا تزيد على (500,000) ريال كل من يخالف أحكام الفقرة (1) من المادة الثلاثين. | Note-level only. Contract reviewers should check that any manpower/outsourcing supplier holds an Annex 4 licence and documents secondments on Ajeer; the client that "deals with" an unlicensed supplier is itself in breach of Annex 4 Art. 70(3). Annex 4 was skimmed, not read article by article. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` (Law Art. 229 bis: `[BOE — Arabic]`) |
| Reg. Art. 11 (Law Art. 36) | A non-Saudi may not be employed in any of 18 listed professions (HR senior administrator, personnel affairs manager, labor affairs manager, personnel relations manager, personnel affairs specialist, personnel clerk, recruitment clerk, HR clerk, timekeeper, general receptionist, hotel receptionist, patient receptionist, complaints clerk, cashier, private security guard, government-relations agent (معقب), key cutter, customs broker), nor may those tasks be assigned to a non-Saudi under another job title; other activities are reserved to Saudis as the Ministry decides. | لا يجوز توظيف العامل غير السعودي في أي من المهن التالية ... كما لا يجوز إسناد أي من مهام تلك المهن والوظائف إلى عامل غير سعودي بطريقة مباشرة أو غير مباشرة تحت أي مسمى وظيفي آخر. | hiring-review must check the SOC title and the actual duties of any non-Saudi hire against this list; an "office administrator" who does payroll and HR files is caught. Later Saudization decisions (e.g. project-management professions from 14 Feb 2027 per the HRSD page) add to this list `[model knowledge — verify]`. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Reg. Art. 12 (Law Art. 37) | A non-Saudi's employment contract is fixed-term however long its term or renewals, and never becomes an indefinite-term contract even if the parties so agree. | يعتبر عقد عمل غير السعودي محدد المدة مهما طالت مدته أو مدد تجديده وفي جميع الأحوال لا يتحول إلى عقد غير محدد المدة حتى لو اتفق الطرفان على ذلك. | Law Art. 55(2) conversion (two renewals or three years) does not apply to expatriates. Annex 5 hides the open-ended option for non-Saudis. termination-review must compute an expatriate's unlawful-termination damages under Law Art. 77(2) (remainder of term), not Art. 77(1). | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Reg. Art. 13 (Law Art. 39) | A non-Saudi whose work the Ministry approves through the Ajeer program procedures is not in breach of Art. 39. | لا يُعد العامل غير السعودي الذي تُقر الوزارة عمله عبر إجراءات برنامج أجير مُخالفاً لحكم المادة. | Secondment of expatriates between entities is lawful only through Ajeer; a bare inter-company loan is an Art. 39 violation (worker repatriated at the expense of the user employer under the old Art. 233; now under the general Art. 229 schedule). | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Reg. Art. 14 First (Law Art. 41) — recruitment | Recruitment may not displace Saudis; the establishment must be in a Nitaqat band that permits recruitment; visas may not push Saudization below the required rate; professions must follow the Saudi occupational classification; no recruitment under 18 or over 60 (experts, doctors and Minister-approved cases excepted); applications go through the Ministry platform; the Ministry may refuse where there is collective wage delay, proven commercial concealment (تستر), workers allowed to work for others or for themselves, Saudization below minimum, false information (five-year recruitment freeze, visa cancellation, criminal referral), visa selling (five-year freeze), or unrenewed work permits/iqamas; no recruitment or transfer without actual work. | لا يجوز أن يؤدي الاستقدام إلى منافسة العمالة السعودية ... للوزارة رفض طلب الاستقدام: إذا تبين وجود تأخر جماعي في دفع الأجور أو ثبوت التستر التجاري ... إذا ثبت قيام المنشأة ببيع تأشيرات العمل الصادرة لها، ويترتب على ذلك إيقاف جميع الإجراءات المتعلقة بالاستقدام لمدة خمس سنوات. | Note-level. The refusal grounds are the same red flags a diligence reviewer looks for: WPS non-compliance, tasattur and visa trading each freeze recruitment. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Reg. Art. 14 Second (1)–(8) (Law Art. 41) — transfer of services | A non-Saudi may transfer to another employer at any time with the current employer's consent (no minimum period unless Nitaqat says otherwise). Transfer without consent is allowed, per Nitaqat controls, for a new arrival without a work permit, for a worker whose permit or iqama has expired, and on expiry of the documented contract (item 7). The Minister or delegate may also approve transfer without consent where: the employer prolongs pending litigation (absent from two hearings in one instance without an excuse accepted by the court, or the court finds delay); on a court's recommendation; the establishment has not paid three consecutive months' wages (worker applies within one Hijri year from the third month's due date); the employer is absent (travel, prison, death) and the establishment cannot meet obligations for three months; special-instruction nationalities; dependants; spousal reunification; the worker reports tasattur with evidence; or public interest. The new employer must meet Saudization; both employers keep the worker's written consent; the electronic consent or attested paper waiver may not be conditioned. | للعامل غير السعودي الانتقال لصاحب عمل آخر دون اشتراط توفر مدة محددة في حال موافقة صاحب العمل الحالي ... يجوز للوزير أو من يفوضه الموافقة على نقل خدمة العامل غير السعودي لصاحب عمل آخر دون موافقة صاحب العمل ... إذا لم تقم المنشأة بدفع أجور العامل المستحقة لثلاثة أشهر متتالية. | Three months of unpaid or late wages gives the worker a statutory exit that also freezes the employer's recruitment (Art. 14 First 12(a)). termination-review should check whether an expatriate resignation is really an Art. 14 Second transfer, which changes the notice and end-of-service analysis. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Reg. Art. 14 Second (21) | Subject to Law Art. 77, a non-Saudi may transfer to another employer without the current employer's consent if (a) twelve months have passed since entry into the Kingdom and (b) the worker notifies the current employer at least ninety days before ending the contractual relationship, unless the parties agree otherwise. | مع مراعاة أحكام المادة (السابعة والسبعون) من النظام، للعامل غير السعودي الانتقال لصاحب العمل آخر دون اشتراط موافقة صاحب العمل الحالي عند توفر الشروط الآتية: أ. أن يكون أمضى اثنا عشر شهراً له من تاريخ دخوله للمملكة. ب. أن يقوم العامل بإشعار صاحب العمل الحالي قبل الانتقال بمدة لا تقل عن (تسعين) يوماً. | New in 2025 (no equivalent in the 2023 English Art. 14). The "subject to Art. 77" proviso means leaving a fixed-term contract early on this route may still expose the worker to the Art. 77(2) remainder-of-term compensation unless the contract fixes a lower amount `[model knowledge — verify]` as to how labor courts apply it. Contract drafters may shorten the 90 days by agreement. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Reg. Art. 14 Second (19)–(20) | Inheritance continuation, change of establishment name, objects, partners or company type with the same commercial register, mergers, partner spin-offs, conversion of a sole establishment into a company, and transfer of ownership with all workers continuing are "name amendments", not transfers of services; moves between branches of the same entity or between entities of the same establishment are "registration transfers". | لا تعتبر الحالات التالية حالات نقل خدمات وإنما حالات تعديل مسمى: ... الاندماج بين منشأتين أو أكثر ... نقل ملكية المنشأة مع استمرار جميع العاملين بالعمل فيها. | Relevant to M&A workforce transfer: a share deal or merger does not require individual worker consents for expatriates on the HRSD side, provided the commercial register continues and MoC approves. Law Art. 18 (successor liability) is not in this file. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Reg. Arts. 15, 15 bis, 16 (Law Arts. 42–44) | Employers must write job descriptions per the Saudi classification, provide training programs, keep training lists, evaluate trainees, disclose training data annually on the Ministry platform, and train Saudis at the percentages the Minister sets; a post-training service bond may not exceed the training duration (indefinite contracts) or the remaining term (fixed contracts); the trainee bears no training cost; the employer may recover training costs only if the worker quits training without legitimate excuse, is dismissed under Law Art. 80 (other than item 6) during training, or resigns or leaves other than under Law Art. 81 during training; training data must be uploaded within 30 days. | في حال اشتراط المنشأة استمرار عمل العامل بعد انتهاء التدريب يجب أن لا يتجاوز هذا الاشتراط المدة المماثلة لمدة برنامج التدريب ... لصاحب العمل تحميل العامل نفقات تدريبه أو تأهيله في الحالات التالية. | A training-bond or clawback clause longer than the course itself is void; clawback is limited to the three listed exits. policy-drafting should cap bonds accordingly. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Reg. Arts. 16 bis (1)–(2) (Law Arts. 47–48) | Student/graduate trainees require a training contract stating duration, dates, profession, roles and obligations; the establishment may pay an allowance; the trainee bears no cost, gets a certificate, and is not bound to work afterwards unless the contract says so; the employer may not end a training contract without compensating the trainee if the contract so provides (except Art. 80 cases); a trainee may end the contract without the Art. 48(2) cost liability where the employer breached the trainee's rights or the trainee was abused. | إبرام عقد تدريب بين المتدرب والمنشأة موضح فيه مدة التدريب ... عدم إلزام المتدرب بالعمل في المنشأة بعد إتمام التدريب مالم ينص عقد التدريب على غير ذلك. | Interns are not employees but have a defined contract; hiring-review should insist on a written training contract for any unpaid intern. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Reg. Art. 18 (Law Arts. 51–52) | The unified model contracts for each contract type in Annex 5 are the approved forms; the employer must document workers' contracts electronically through the Ministry's approved platform. | تعتمد النماذج الموحدة لعقد العمل بأنواعه بالصيغ المرافقة لهذه اللائحة (الملحق رقم 5). يجب على صاحب العمل توثيق عقود العاملين إلكترونياً عبر المنصة المعتمدة لدى الوزارة. | Documentation is mandatory, not optional (the 2023 English Art. 18 only required the contract to "at least include the obligatory clauses"). An undocumented contract is a scheduled violation and, per the amendment-watch leads, loses Saudization credit from 15 Apr 2026 `[model knowledge — verify]`. The platform is Qiwa `[model knowledge — verify]`. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Law Art. 52(1) (M/44 1446H) | The Ministry's model for each type of contract must contain: employer name and place; worker name and nationality; proof of identity; residence address; agreed wage including benefits and allowances; type and place of work; date of joining; term if fixed; and the basic rights and obligations of each party. Parties may add clauses that do not conflict with the Law, Regulations and decisions (Art. 52(2)). | تضع الوزارة نموذجاً موحداً لكل نوع من أنواع عقد العمل، يحتوي بصورة أساسية على: اسم صاحب العمل ومكانه، واسم العامل وجنسيته، وما يلزم لإثبات شخصيته، وعنوان إقامته، والأجر المتفق عليه بما في ذلك المزايا والبدلات، ونوع العمل ومكانه، وتاريخ الالتحاق به، ومدة العقد إن كان محدد المدة، وحقوق كل طرف والتزاماته الأساسية. | Read from the M/44 amending block of the [معدلة] article in `boe/labor-law-ar.md`; the article body above it is the 2005 text. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic]` |
| Annex 5 permanent contract cls. 1–4 | Mandatory data: contract number; type (fixed or open-ended, from a drop-down; open-ended not shown for non-Saudis); execution date; start date; end date (fixed); place of execution; employer's name, type, HRSD establishment number, unified national number, national address, phone, email, signatory, capacity and capacity document; worker's name, nationality, ID type and number, passport (non-Saudi), gender, marital status, date of birth, national address, mobile, email; job title, work domain (inside KSA), city and work location, work type. | بيانات العقد ... بيانات الطرف الأول ... بيانات الطرف الثاني ... المهنة ومعلومات العمل. تعتبر البيانات المذكورة في البنود أعلاه جزءاً لا يتجزأ من هذا العقد. | These are the fields Qiwa forces; a paper "offer letter" that omits them is not the contract of record. hiring-review should reconcile the offer letter against the Annex 5 fields before documentation. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Annex 5 cl. 5 (term) | Three alternative term clauses: open-ended from the start date (Saudis only); fixed term ending on a stated date; or fixed term that renews automatically for an equal, equal-successive, or specified period unless a party notifies non-renewal through the Portal at least (…) days before expiry. | يسري هذا العقد لمدة غير محددة ... / يسري هذا العقد لمدة (تحدد مدة العقد) ... / ويتجدد تلقائياً (لمدة مماثلة أو لمدد مماثلة أو تحدد مدة أخرى)، ما لم يخطر أحد الطرفين الطرف الآخر بعدم رغبته بالتجديد من خلال المنصة وذلك قبل (...) يوماً من تاريخ نهاية العقد. | The non-renewal notice must go through the Portal (cl. 14.1) to count. renewal-tracker-style logic for employment: diarise expiry minus the stated notice days. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Annex 5 cl. 6 and Reg. Art. 19 (Law Art. 53, M/44) | Probation must be stated expressly in the contract with its duration; the total may not exceed 180 days in any case; it may be split into several consecutive periods if stated clearly at signing; Eid al-Fitr, Eid al-Adha, National Day, Founding Day and sick leave do not count; either party may end the contract during probation via the Portal. | يجب النص صراحة في عقد العمل على تحديد مدة التجربة المتفق عليها على ألا تتجاوز مدة التجربة 180 يوماً ويجوز تقسيم مدة التجربة إلى مُدد متعددة، شريطة أن تكون هذه المُدد متصلة ... لا يدخل في حساب مدة التجربة إجازة عيدي الفطر والأضحى، وإجازة اليوم الوطني، وإجازة يوم التأسيس، والإجازة المرضية. | The 2023 English Art. 19 (90 days, extendable by written agreement to 180) is superseded: 180 is now the single cap and there is no separate extension step. Termination during probation needs no notice or award (Law Art. 80(6)); the contract-form drop-down and the Portal termination are the evidence. termination-review must add excluded days before deciding whether probation had expired. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Annex 5 cl. 7 | Working days per week and daily or weekly working hours are filled in according to the employer's adopted standard, plus the number of weekly rest days. | تحدد أيام العمل العادية بـ (عدد أيام العمل) أيام في الأسبوع وتحدد ساعات العمل (اليومية/الأسبوعية) بـ (عدد ساعات العمل) ... ويحق للطرف الثاني (عدد أيام الراحة) يوم راحة أسبوعية. | The statutory ceilings are Law Art. 98 (8 hours/day or 48/week; 6/36 in Ramadan for Muslims) and Art. 101 (no more than five consecutive hours without a 30-minute break, no more than 12 hours at the workplace) — read from BOE. wage-hour-qa should compare the contract figure to these ceilings, and to Reg. Art. 23 for exempt categories. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Annex 5 cl. 8 and Annex 1 Arts. 33–37 (Law Arts. 109–111) | Annual leave of not less than 21 days, rising to not less than 30 days after five consecutive years, paid in advance; the establishment fixes leave dates per work needs with at least 30 days' notice; leave must be taken in its year and may not be waived or cashed during service; the worker may defer with consent; the employer may postpone up to 90 days after the entitlement year and, with written consent, to the end of the following year; untaken accrued leave is paid out on termination. | يستحق الطرف الثاني عن كل عام إجازة سنوية مدفوعة الأجر مقدماً ومدتها (عدد أيام الإجازة) يوم ... لا يسقط حق الطرف الثاني في الحصول على أجرة عن أيام الإجازات المستحقة التي لم يتمتع بها ... للطرف الأول تأجيل الإجازة السنوية بعد نهاية سنة استحقاقها إذا اقتضت ظروف العمل ذلك لمدة لا تزيد على (90) يوماً. | Annex 5 cl. 8.1 defines "day" for annual leave as a working day, unlike every other "day" in the form (calendar). log-leave and leave-tracker should carry the distinction. A "use it or lose it" policy is void; unused leave is a liability on the balance sheet (diligence). | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Annex 5 cl. 9–10 (wage structure) | Wage table: basic wage, housing allowance, transport allowance, other cash allowances, total wage (in figures and words, SAR), GOSI deduction percentage, net wage; each with a due date (monthly or a specified date; weekly per contract type). Optional: commissions (percentage, reason, entitlement period) and in-kind benefits. Net wage is paid through the HRSD-approved payment means. Bank name and IBAN are contract data. Allowances and benefits are optional and by agreement. | يلتزم الطرف الأول بسداد صافي الأجر المستحق من خلال وسيلة السداد المعتمدة لدى وزارة الموارد البشرية والتنمية الاجتماعية ... (ملاحظة: البدلات والمزايا يتم تحديدها (اختيارياً) حسب اتفاق الأطراف). | Law Art. 61(5)–(6) as amended by M/44 requires housing and transport or a cash allowance "included in their wage"; the form's housing/transport lines are how that is evidenced. The basic/allowance split drives overtime (basic only, Law Art. 107) and end-of-service award (last wage — total, subject to Art. 86 carve-out for commissions). wage-hour-qa must read the split from the documented contract. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Annex 5 cl. 11 (employer obligations) | Pay the wage in cl. 9 and document payment on the HRSD-approved wage platform; pay commissions and deliver in-kind benefits on due dates; assign overtime in writing or electronically and pay hourly wage plus 50% of basic hourly wage, or with the worker's written/electronic consent grant compensatory leave per the Regulations; not exceed the overtime ceiling except with the worker's consent; provide preventive and curative health care per the Cooperative Health Insurance Law; register the worker with GOSI and pay contributions; for non-Saudis, bear recruitment, iqama and work-permit fees and renewals, delay fines caused by the employer, profession-change fees, exit/re-entry fees and the return ticket (not where the worker is unfit or leaves without legitimate reason); grant annual leave, holidays, sick and other statutory leave; return the worker's documents; pay wages and settle entitlements within one week of the end of the contract, or within two weeks if the worker ended it; pay end-of-service award within the same period, except termination in probation, resignation with under two consecutive years, or Art. 80 termination; pay task expenses. | يلتزم الطرف الأول بدفع أجر الطرف الثاني حسب المذكور في البند (9)، وتوثيق الدفع عبر منصة الأجور المعتمدة لدى وزارة الموارد البشرية والتنمية الاجتماعية ... يلتزم الطرف الأول بدفع أجر الطرف الثاني وتصفية حقوقه خلال أسبوع - كحد أقصى - من تاريخ انتهاء العقد، وفي حال الإنهاء من الطرف الثاني فيلتزم الطرف الأول بدفع أجر الطرف الثاني وتصفية حقوقه خلال مدة لا تزيد عن أسبوعين. | The "wage platform" is the Wage Protection System channel (Mudad) `[model knowledge — verify]`. The one-week/two-week settlement windows restate Law Art. 88. termination-review's final-settlement checklist: wages to date, untaken leave (cl. 8.2), overtime and compensatory leave balance (Reg. Art. 22 bis(4)), end-of-service award, return ticket (non-Saudi), document return. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Annex 5 cl. 12 (worker obligations) | Perform the work per professional standards and lawful instructions; care for tools and materials and return unused materials; good conduct, compliance with Saudi laws, customs and the employer's rules, bearing fines for breaching them; assist without extra pay in disasters; undergo medical examinations before or during employment for occupational or communicable diseases. | يلتزم الطرف الثاني بإنجاز العمل الموكل إليه؛ وفقاً لأصول المهنة ووفقاً لتعليمات الطرف الأول ... يلتزم الطرف الثاني - عند طلب الطرف الأول - بأداء الفحوصات الطبية. | Mirrors Law Art. 65. The medical-examination duty supports fitness-for-duty checks, subject to the occupational-fitness regulation (Decision 33232 of 11/3/1447H, not read). | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Annex 5 cl. 13 (governing law and disputes) | The Labor Law, its Regulations, ministerial decisions and the HRSD-approved work regulations govern the contract and any gap; the contract supersedes prior oral or written agreements; Saudi law governs; the contract is an executive instrument (سند تنفيذي) and the Enforcement Court has jurisdiction over the employer's obligation to pay the net wage in cl. 9.1.1.7; every other dispute, including additional terms, is first resolved by friendly settlement and, failing settlement, by the labor courts of the Kingdom. | يعد هذا العقد سنداً تنفيذياً، وينعقد الاختصاص لمحكمة التنفيذ فيما يلي: التزام الطرف الأول بدفع صافي الأجر المستحق ... فإن كل نزاع أو خلاف ينشأ عن هذا العقد ... يتم حلّه ابتداءً من خلال التسوية الودية، وفي حال تعذر الوصول إلى تسوية، فينعقد الاختصاص بنظر النزاع للمحاكم العمالية. | This clause is the documentary basis for the "direct enforcement of the wage clause" route (see `labor-dispute-route.md`). Only the net wage line is enforceable directly; allowances outside cl. 9.1.1, commissions, in-kind benefits, overtime and end-of-service award still go through friendly settlement and the labor courts. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Annex 5 cls. 14–15 (general and additional terms) | Notices and any act relating to the contract have legal effect only if made through the Portal's services, means or forms and documented there (fallback to national address, registered mail, phone, email or hand delivery only where no Portal service exists); the worker consents to the GOSI deduction; additional terms may be added but are void if they conflict with the form, the Law, the Regulations or the approved work regulations; Gregorian calendar; Arabic prevails over any other language; specified data (contract type, job and location, annual leave, wage and benefits, bank account) may be amended by both parties' consent through the Portal and the employer must document the amendment; the contract is an electronic counterpart signed electronically; the Portal may share contract and financial-transaction data. Cl. 15 suggests optional clauses: termination provisions (mutual agreement with the worker's written/electronic consent, unilateral termination of an indefinite contract, Art. 80 termination), intellectual property, confidentiality and non-competition. | اتفق الطرفان على أن الإشعارات والإخطارات وأي تصرفات تصدر لأي غرض ... لن تكون منتجة لآثارها القانونية إلا إذا تمّت بواسطة الخدمات أو الوسائل أو النماذج التي تعتمدها المنصة ... يجوز للطرفين الاتفاق على إضافة شروط وأحكام إضافية بشرط عدم تعارضها ... وفي حال تعارضها تعد الشروط الإضافية ملغية. | A termination or resignation notice sent only by email is, on the face of cl. 14.1, ineffective if a Portal service exists for it; termination-review must ask for the Qiwa record. Side letters that improve on the form survive only if they do not conflict (Law Art. 8: more-beneficial terms stand). The Gregorian election displaces Law Art. 10's Hijri default. Non-compete clauses must meet Law Art. 83 (written, limited in time, place and type of work, max two years). | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Annex 1 Arts. 6–7 | The contract is drawn up in two Arabic copies per the Ministry's unified form and documented as the Law and Regulations require; it may also be drawn in another language but the Arabic text always prevails; the establishment may cancel the contract of a worker who fails to start without legitimate excuse within seven working days of signing (contracted inside KSA) or of arrival (contracted abroad). | يتم توظيف العامل بموجب عقد عمل يحرر من نسختين باللغة العربية وفقاً للنموذج الموحد ... يحق للمنشأة إلغاء عقد العامل الذي لا يباشر مهام عمله دون عذر مشروع خلال سبعة أيام عمل من تاريخ التوقيع على العقد. | The seven-working-day no-show cancellation is the clean exit for a candidate who never starts; after that the probation route applies. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Annex 1 Arts. 15–17 and Law Art. 90 (M/46 1436H) — wage payment | Subject to any procedures or arrangements of the Wage Protection Program, wages are paid in the official currency on a stated date and deposited in workers' accounts through banks approved in the Kingdom; overtime wages are paid at the end of the month of the assignment; if pay day falls on the weekly rest or an official holiday, payment is made on the preceding working day. Law Art. 90 as amended: daily-paid workers at least weekly, monthly-paid once a month, piece work needing over two weeks paid weekly in proportion; establishments are obliged to pay wages into workers' accounts through approved banks by the due dates, the Minister may exempt some establishments. | مع مراعاة أي إجراءات أو ترتيبات ينص عليها برنامج حماية الأجور؛ تدفع أجور العمال بالعملة الرسمية للبلاد في تاريخ .../.../... وتودع في حسابات العمال عن طريق البنوك المعتمدة في المملكة ... تلزم المنشآت بدفع الأجور في حسابات العمال عن طريق البنوك المعتمدة في المملكة. | Bank payment is mandatory, not optional (the 2005 text of Art. 90(2), printed as the original text of the [معدلة] article in `boe/labor-law-ar.md`, made it subject to the worker's consent; the M/46 wording was read from the amending block). The Wage Protection System itself (monthly wage-file upload to Mudad, matching against GOSI and Qiwa data, compliance percentage, escalating service suspensions and fines for non-compliance) is a ministerial-decision regime not contained in the Regulations `[model knowledge — verify]`. Late or unpaid wages: Law Art. 94 lets the worker, representative or labor-office director apply for an order to pay and a fine up to double the late amount (read from BOE, unamended text). | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` (Law Art. 90: `[BOE — Arabic]`) |
| Reg. Art. 20 (Law Art. 58) | A contract clause fixing the workplace as anywhere in the Kingdom, or allowing relocation that requires a change of residence per work needs, is deemed the worker's written consent to such relocation. | إذا تضمن عقد العمل شرطاً يحدد مكان عمل العامل في أي مكان بالمملكة أو يجيز لصاحب العمل نقل العامل ... يعد ذلك موافقة كتابية من العامل على نقل مكان عمله. | A mobility clause in cl. 15 additional terms is effective; without it, relocation needs fresh written consent (Law Art. 58(1)) except emergency assignments up to 30 days a year at the employer's cost (Art. 58(2)). | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Reg. Art. 21 (Law Art. 61) | "Forced labor" means work or services imposed on the worker under threat of penalty, not provided in the contract, and not performed voluntarily, excluding emergencies and force majeure; Law Art. 61(5) (housing or cash allowance) applies to private-sector and non-profit-sector workers. | يقصد بعبارة "تشغيل العامل سخرة": جميع الأعمال أو الخدمات التي تفرض عنوة على العامل ولم ينص عليها في عقد العمل وتتم تحت التهديد بأي عقاب ... تطبق الفقرة الخامسة على العاملين في القطاع الخاص والقطاع غير الربحي. | Confirms that the housing obligation (or allowance) is not limited to expatriates or to remote sites. Law Art. 61(4)–(6) are M/44 additions, read from the amending block in `boe/labor-law-ar.md`. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Reg. Art. 22 (Law Art. 106) | Overtime hours may not exceed 720 hours per year; more is allowed with the worker's consent. Law Art. 106 caps actual hours in the listed exceptional cases at 10 per day or 60 per week. | لا يجوز أن تزيد ساعات العمل الإضافية خلال السنة على سبعمائة وعشرين ساعة؛ ويجوز بموافقة العامل زيادة عدد الساعات الإضافية عن ذلك. | The 2023 English Art. 22 prints "27 hours per year", which does not match the Arabic "سبعمائة وعشرين" (720); treat the English figure as a transcription error. Annex 5 cl. 11.4.2 repeats the cap and the consent exception. wage-hour-qa should test annual overtime against 720 and check for documented consent above it. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Reg. Art. 22 bis (Law Art. 107(1), M/44) | With the worker's consent, paid compensatory leave may replace overtime pay: the parties agree the assignment period and the leave amount, which may not be less than one and a half hours of leave per overtime hour; the employer may schedule the leave within 60 days of the overtime unless otherwise agreed; compensatory leave may not exceed 30 days in a year; the worker is paid for accrued compensatory leave if leaving before using it. | تكون الإجازة التعويضية عن ساعات العمل الإضافية وفق ما يتفق عليه الطرفان ... بشرط ألا يقل مقدارها عن ساعة ونصف إجازة عن كل ساعة عمل ... لا يجوز في جميع الأحوال أن تزيد الإجازة التعويضية خلال السنة على 30 يوم. للعامل حق الحصول على أجر الإجازات التعويضية المستحقة إذا ترك العمل قبل استعماله لها. | New in 2025. "Time off in lieu" policies are lawful only at 1.5:1 or better, capped at 30 days a year, with the balance paid out on exit. leave-tracker should carry a compensatory-leave balance with a 60-day scheduling clock. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Reg. Art. 23 (Law Art. 108) | Definitions of preparatory and complementary work (combined maximum 30 minutes added to working hours, 15 each), intermittent work (actual hours 10 per day, 8 in Ramadan, 48 per week, 36 in Ramadan for Muslims, with at least 10 consecutive rest hours in 24), and guards and cleaners (12 hours per day, 10 in Ramadan, same weekly caps; cleaners not more than six consecutive actual hours); civil security guards are not "guards" for this purpose; excess is overtime. Senior managers with the employer's authority over workers are exempt from Arts. 98 and 101 by the Law itself. | تحدد ساعات العمل الفعلية في الأعمال التي تكون متقطعة بالضرورة بعشر ساعات في اليوم ... تحدد ساعات العمل الفعلية للعمال المخصصين للحراسة والنظافة باثنتي عشرة ساعة في اليوم ... وما زاد على ذلك يحسب عملاً إضافياً. | The only overtime-exempt category with no hours ceiling is the senior-manager category in Law Art. 108(1); drivers, technicians, loading staff and guards have their own ceilings and earn overtime above them. wage-hour-qa should not accept a blanket "exempt" label for guards or drivers. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Reg. Art. 24 and Annex 1 Art. 39 (Law Art. 112) | Paid public holidays: Eid al-Fitr four days from the day after 29 Ramadan (Umm al-Qura); Eid al-Adha four days from the Day of Arafah; National Day one day (first day of Libra); Founding Day one day (22 February). Overlaps: with weekly rest the worker is compensated with an equivalent day before or after; annual leave is extended by the holiday days; during sick leave the worker receives full pay for the holiday days; National Day or Founding Day falling within an Eid holiday is not compensated. | إجازة عيد الفطر لمدة أربعة أيام ... إجازة عيد الأضحى لمدة أربعة أيام تبدأ من يوم الوقوف بعرفة ... إجازة اليوم الوطني ... إجازة يوم التأسيس لمدة يوم واحد في يوم الثاني والعشرين من شهر فبراير. | The 2023 English Art. 24 has no Founding Day and no annual-leave extension for a Founding Day overlap. leave-tracker and log-leave should add holiday days to any annual leave that spans them. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Reg. Art. 25 and Annex 1 Art. 38 (Law Art. 116) | Unpaid leave requires the employer's consent; where the agreed unpaid leave exceeds twenty days the contract is suspended and all its effects stop unless otherwise agreed; a fixed-term contract is extended by the suspension period unless otherwise agreed. | إذا تجاوزت مدة الإجازة بدون أجر - المتفق عليها - عشرين يوماً؛ وأصبح عقد العمل موقوفاً، فإن جميع الآثار المترتبة على عقد العمل تتوقف تبعاً لذلك ... إذا كان عقد العمل محدد المدة فيمدد بمقدار مدة توقف العقد. | Suspension stops service accrual for end-of-service award and leave `[model knowledge — verify]` as to how courts treat GOSI and medical insurance during suspension. leave-tracker should flag day 21 of unpaid leave. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Reg. Art. 26 and Annex 1 Art. 41 (Law Art. 117) | Sick leave in a year counted from the first sick leave: first 30 days full pay, next 60 days three-quarters pay, next 30 days unpaid, continuous or intermittent, proven by a certificate from the establishment's doctor or an approved medical body; the worker may join annual leave to sick leave; sick leave falling during annual leave suspends the annual leave, which resumes afterwards; weekly rest days falling in sick leave are not compensated. | للعامل الذي يثبت مرضه الحق في إجازة مرضية بأجر عن الثلاثين يوماً الأولى، وبثلاثة أرباع الأجر عن الستين يوماً التالية، ودون أجر للثلاثين يوماً التي تلي ذلك ... إذا وقعت أيام الإجازة المرضية أثناء أيام الإجازة السنوية فتوقف أيام الإجازة السنوية إلى حين انتهاء الإجازة المرضية. | Law Art. 82 bars termination for illness before the sick-leave entitlement is exhausted (read from BOE). leave-tracker should start the 120-day clock at the first sick day of the cycle, not on 1 January. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Reg. Art. 27 First (Law Art. 120) — part-time | A part-time contract must be written and fixed-term, stating hours that are less than half the establishment's usual daily hours (daily or on some days of the week); renewable for an equal or agreed term; termination by either party without legitimate reason entitles the injured party to the wages for the remainder of the term as compensation unless otherwise agreed; part-timers are subject to the Law's rules on leave, weekly rest, official holidays and overtime; a Saudi part-timer counts toward Saudization per Nitaqat if registered with GOSI as part-time. | يجب أن يكون عقد العمل لبعض الوقت مكتوباً ومحدد المدة؛ وينص فيه على ساعات العمل بحيث تقل عن نصف ساعات العمل اليومية المعتادة لدى المنشأة ... يخضع العاملون لبعض الوقت لأحكام نظام العمل فيما يتعلق بالإجازات والراحة الأسبوعية والعطل الرسمية والعمل الإضافي. | Annex 5 contains a separate part-time form (نموذج عقد عمل لبعض الوقت) with mandatory and optional clauses. worker-classification: a "part-timer" working half or more of normal hours is a full-time worker. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Reg. Art. 27 Second — flexible work (العمل المرن) | Flexible work is non-full-time work for one or more employers paid by the hour, with hours per employer less than half the establishment's hours; restricted to Saudis; the employer owes no paid leave of any kind (annual, occasion, sick) and no end-of-service award; no probation; GOSI pension and occupational-hazards branches apply per GOSI rules; Nitaqat counts one point per 160 completed flexible hours; wages are hourly, paid monthly or as agreed; hours above 95 per month with one employer are overtime (by agreement payable at the base hourly rate), and the worker may not exceed 160 hours per month with one employer; the worker may accept or refuse any call without sanction; the contract with one employer may not exceed one year (continuous or not), after which the employer may extend with consent or conclude a full Labor Law contract; Law Art. 83 non-compete applies; the contract must be electronic, fixed-term, hourly, documented on the Ministry portal; employing on flexible work without a documented contract is penalised under Ministerial Decision 178743 of 27/9/1440H; approved service providers are listed on the portal; rest-period rules apply; labor courts hear flexible-work disputes (Third). | يقصد بالعمل المرن: العمل الذي يؤديه عامل غير متفرغ لدى صاحب عمل أو أكثر ويكون احتساب الأجر على أساس الساعة ... تقتصر عقود العمل بنظام العمل المرن على السعوديين فقط ... لا يلزم صاحب العمل تعويض العامل بعقد بنظام (العمل المرن) بمكافأة نهاية الخدمة ... يجب ألا تتجاوز مدة عقد العمل بتنظيم (العمل المرن) لدى صاحب عمل واحد عن سنة. | New in 2025 (the 2023 English Art. 27 has only the part-time rules). worker-classification: a non-Saudi cannot be on flexible work; a flexible-work arrangement past one year or past 160 hours a month converts the analysis to an ordinary contract. Remote work is not regulated here; the Regulations contain no remote-work article (the HRSD remote-work program is a separate ministerial scheme `[model knowledge — verify]`). | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Reg. Art. 28 (Law Art. 141) | Where the establishment is not covered by the GOSI occupational-hazards branch: the employer reports a work injury to the competent labor office within one week of learning of it; the office decides whether it is a work injury on official reports, refers the worker to a government hospital for a disability-percentage report if none exists or if contested, determines compensation from the disability percentage, and refers refusals to the labor courts. | يقوم صاحب العمل بإبلاغ مكتب العمل المختص عن إصابة عامل لديه خلال أسبوع من تاريخ علمه بها ... إذا رفض أحد الطرفين ما حدده مكتب العمل يحال الموضوع إلى المحاكم العمالية المختصة للفصل فيه. | See `occupational-safety.md`. For GOSI-covered establishments the GOSI reporting rules apply instead `[model knowledge — verify]` as to GOSI's own deadline. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Reg. Arts. 29–30 (Law Arts. 142, 146) | First-aid cabinet with a listed minimum inventory (gauze, bandages, tourniquet, antiseptic, eye-wash, stretcher, airway kit, splints, spinal board, cervical collar, scissors, blanket, forceps), kept usable, replenished, marked with a red crescent on white, location and responsible person posted; remote locations are sites more than 50 km (paved road) or 25 km (unpaved) from the urban boundary, or settlements without utilities and services. | على صاحب العمل أن يعد في مكان العمل خزانة للإسعافات الطبية ... تحدد الأماكن البعيدة عن العمران: مواقع العمل التي تبتعد عن النطاق العمراني ... بمسافة تزيد على خمسين كيلو متراً إذا كانت الطريق معبدة؛ ومسافة خمسة وعشرين كيلو متراً إذا كانت الطريق غير معبدة. | Detail in `occupational-safety.md`. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Reg. Art. 31 and Annex 1 Art. 51 (Law Art. 154) | A working mother returning from maternity leave may take paid nursing breaks totalling not more than one hour a day, counted as actual working hours, for 24 months from delivery, whether breastfeeding or not; the break is in addition to ordinary rest periods; without an on-site nursery she chooses the hour at the start or end of the day, with a nursery she may split it; she must notify the employer in writing of the time and any change. | يحق للمرأة العاملة الحصول على فترة أو فترات استراحة بقصد إرضاع مولودها مدفوعة الأجر لا تزيد في مجموعها عن الساعة في اليوم الواحد ... وذلك لمدة أربعة وعشرين شهراً من تاريخ الوضع. | The 24-month duration is a regulation-level addition; the Law article is silent on duration. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Annex 1 Art. 50 (Law Art. 151, M/44) | Maternity leave of twelve weeks at full pay, six of which must follow delivery; the other six may be distributed from four weeks before the expected date; if late delivery leaves fewer than six weeks, the balance is unpaid; in all cases the leave may be extended by one month unpaid; a mother of a sick or disabled child needing constant care has one further month at full pay after maternity leave, extendable by one unpaid month. | للمرأة العاملة الحق في إجازة وضع بأجر كامل لمدة (اثني عشر) أسبوعاً، منها وجوبياً الأسابيع الستة التالية للوضع ... وفي جميع الأحوال يحق للمرأة العاملة تمديد هذه الإجازة (شهراً) دون أجر. | Law Art. 155 (M/134 1440H) bars dismissal or warning of dismissal during pregnancy and maternity leave, including illness arising from either, up to 180 days' absence a year (read from the M/134 amending block in `boe/labor-law-ar.md`). Pre-2025 handbooks saying ten weeks are void under Reg. Art. 4(2). | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Annex 1 Art. 40 (Law Art. 113, M/44) | Paid leave of five days on marriage; three days on the birth of a child, taken within seven days of the birth; five days on the death of a spouse, ascendant or descendant, from the date of death; three days on the death of a brother or sister; four months and ten days (iddah) for a Muslim widow, extendable unpaid if pregnant until delivery; fifteen days for a non-Muslim widow; the establishment may require supporting documents. | خمسة أيام عند زواجه. ثلاثة أيام في حالة والدة مولود له خلال (سبعة) أيام من تاريخ الولادة. خمسة أيام في حالة وفاة زوجة العامل أو أحد أصوله أو فروعه ... ثلاثة أيام في حالة وفاة الأخ أو الأخت. | The sibling-bereavement day count and the seven-day window for paternity leave are 2025 additions (M/44). log-leave categories should match this list. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Annex 1 Arts. 42–44 (Law Arts. 114–115) | Paid leave on dialysis days on a medical report; examination leave (paid for a non-repeated year if the employer approved enrolment; otherwise from annual leave or unpaid; 15 days' notice; documents may be required); Hajj leave of 10 to 15 days including Eid al-Adha, once in service, after two consecutive years, subject to the establishment's annual quota. | يحق للعامل المريض بفشل كلوي إجازة مدفوعة الأجر في اليوم الذي يجرى له فيه الغسيل الكلوي ... للعامل الحق في الحصول على إجازة بأجر لا تقل مدتها عن عشرة أيام ولا تزيد على خمسة عشر يوماً بما فيها إجازة عيد الأضحى؛ وذلك لأداء فريضة الحج لمرة واحدة. | Dialysis leave exists only in the model regulations, not in the Law. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Annex 1 Arts. 53–56 (conduct, harassment) | The establishment must set dress-code rules (Sharia-compliant, professional, modest and non-transparent, with penalties, published and acknowledged); workers must observe Sharia and social norms; no khalwa (being alone with the opposite sex) and the establishment must take measures to prevent it; all forms of physical, verbal or suggestive abuse, harassment or coercion are prohibited even in jest; "abuse" includes exploitation, blackmail, enticement or threat, physical, psychological or sexual, by anyone at the workplace, and assisting or concealing it; a victim may complain to the establishment within five working days (or to the government authority if the abuser is the owner or top authority), witnesses may report; a committee formed by decision of the competent official investigates and recommends a disciplinary penalty within five working days; the committee hears parties and witnesses confidentially, keeps signed minutes, may separate complainant and respondent, refers crimes to the general manager for reporting, may recommend a penalty for a malicious complaint; internal penalties do not bar recourse to the authorities and vice versa. | مع عدم الإخلال بحق من وقع عليه الإيذاء في مكان العمل من الالتجاء إلى الجهات الحكومية المختصة، يحق له التقدم بشكواه للمنشأة خلال مدة أقصاها خمسة أيام عمل من وقوع الإيذاء عليه ... على المنشأة عند تقديم شكوى أو بلاغ تشكيل لجنة ... وذلك خلال خمسة أيام عمل من تلقيها الشكوى. | This is the mandatory internal-investigation procedure for harassment in every establishment that adopted the model. internal-investigation should run to these steps (five-day complaint window, committee, confidentiality, signed minutes, separation, criminal referral) and note the Anti-Harassment Law (M/96 of 1439H) as the criminal overlay `[model knowledge — verify]`. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Annex 1 Art. 57 (Law Art. 74, M/46 and M/44) | The contract ends: by written agreement (worker's consent in writing); on expiry of a fixed term unless expressly renewed; by either party's will in an indefinite contract per Law Art. 75; by resignation per Law Art. 79 bis; on reaching retirement age under the Social Insurance Law unless the parties agree to continue; force majeure; permanent closure of the establishment; ending of the activity the worker works in, unless otherwise agreed; a final decision or judgment of the competent court ending the contract in bankruptcy proceedings; any other case provided by another law. | ينتهي عقد العمل في أي من الأحوال الآتية: ... الاستقالة وفق التفصيل الوارد في المادة (التاسعة والسبعون مكرر) من النظام ... صدور قرار أو حكم نهائي من المحكمة المختصة؛ بإنهاء عقد العامل في أي من إجراءات الإفلاس المفتتحة وفق نظام الإفلاس. | The original text of the [معدلة] article in `boe/labor-law-ar.md` is the 2005 list (five grounds, retirement at 60/55); its amending blocks give the M/46 (eight grounds), M/134 (retirement per GOSI law) and M/44 (resignation, bankruptcy) versions, all read today. termination-review must identify which ground is invoked before reaching notice and award. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` (Law Art. 74: `[BOE — Arabic]`) |
| Law Art. 75 (M/44 1446H) | Indefinite contract, monthly wage: the worker gives at least 30 days' written notice; the employer gives at least 60 days' written notice; both for a legitimate reason. Indefinite contract, wage not monthly: 30 days for either party. Art. 76 (M/46): the party not observing notice pays the other the worker's wage for the notice period, unless a higher amount is agreed. Art. 78 (M/46): during employer-initiated notice the worker may take one paid day a week or eight hours a week to seek work; the employer may release the worker from work during notice with service continuing and notice-period wages due. | إذا كان العقد غير محدد المدة وكان الأجر يدفع شهرياً ... أ- إذا كان الإنهاء من طرف العامل، فيجب عليه أن يوجه إشعاراً كتابياً بذلك لصاحب العمل قبل (ثلاثين) يوماً على الأقل. ب- إذا كان الإنهاء من طرف صاحب العمل، فيجب عليه أن يوجه إشعاراً كتابياً بذلك للعامل قبل (ستين) يوماً على الأقل. | Read from the M/44 amending block in `boe/labor-law-ar.md`; the original text (30/15 days) and the intermediate M/46 text (60/30 days) precede it. The asymmetry is new: employer 60, worker 30. Contract clauses providing 30 days for the employer are below the floor. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic]` |
| Law Art. 79 bis (M/44 1446H) — resignation | A resignation is deemed accepted if the employer does not respond within 30 days of submission; the employer may defer acceptance for not more than 60 days where work interest requires, by a reasoned written explanation given to the worker before the 30 days lapse, the deferral running from the date of the explanation; the contract ends on acceptance, on lapse of the 30 days without response, or on lapse of the deferral; the worker may withdraw within seven days of submission unless already accepted; a resignation may not carry a deferred date; the contract remains in force and both parties perform during the resignation period; a worker whose contract ends by resignation receives all rights under the Law. Law Art. 2 (M/44) defines resignation as the worker's written, uncoerced, unconditional expression of the wish to end a fixed-term contract, and the employer's acceptance. | يُعد طلب الاستقالة المقدم مقبولاً إذا مضى على تقديمه (ثلاثون) يوماً دون ردٍّ من صاحب العمل. ولصاحب العمل تأجيل قبول طلب الاستقالة مدة لا تزيد على (ستين) يوماً ... للعامل العدول عن طلب الاستقالة خلال مدة لا تتجاوز (سبعة) أيام من تاريخ تقديمه ... لا يصح أن يُحدد في طلب الاستقالة تاريخ مؤجل لها. | The Art. 2 definition ties "resignation" to fixed-term contracts, while Art. 74(3 bis) and Annex 1 Art. 57(4) list it as a general ground; how the labor courts reconcile this with Art. 75 notice for indefinite contracts is open `[model knowledge — verify]`. termination-review: the exit date is a computed date (submission + 30, or acceptance date, or explanation date + up to 60), and end-of-service award on resignation follows Art. 85 fractions unless Art. 87 applies. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic]` |
| Law Art. 77 (M/46 1436H) | Unless the contract fixes a specific compensation for termination by either party for an illegitimate reason, the injured party is entitled to: 15 days' wage for each year of service (indefinite contract); the wage for the remainder of the term (fixed contract); in both cases not less than two months' wage. | ما لم يتضمن العقد تعويضاً محدداً مقابل إنهائه من أحد الطرفين لسبب غير مشروع، يستحق الطرف المتضرر من إنهاء العقد تعويضاً على النحو الآتي: أجر خمسة عشر يوماً عن كل سنة من سنوات خدمة العامل إذا كان العقد غير محدد المدة؛ أجر المدة الباقية من العقد إذا كان العقد محدد المدة؛ يجب ألا يقل التعويض عن أجر العامل لمدة شهرين. | Read from the M/46 amending block in `boe/labor-law-ar.md`; the original text is the 2005 discretionary-damages rule. Contractual liquidated amounts below two months are applied by some courts and rejected by others `[model knowledge — verify]`. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic]` |
| Law Art. 80 (M/46 1436H) | Termination without award, notice or compensation only in nine cases, after giving the worker the chance to state objections: assault on the employer, manager, superiors or subordinates; failure of essential obligations, disobedience of lawful orders, or deliberate breach of posted safety instructions despite written warning; proven bad conduct or act against honour or honesty; deliberate act or omission to cause material loss (reported to the authorities within 24 hours); forgery to obtain the job; probation; unexcused absence over 30 days in a contract year or over 15 consecutive days, with a written warning after 20 days (first case) or 10 days (second); unlawful exploitation of position; disclosure of industrial or commercial secrets. | لا يجوز لصاحب العمل فسخ العقد دون مكافأة العامل أو إشعاره أو تعويضه إلا في الحالات الآتية ... إذا تغيب العامل دون سبب مشروع أكثر من ثلاثين يوماً خلال السنة العقدية الواحدة أو أكثر من خمسة عشر يوماً متتالية، على أن يسبق الفصل إنذار كتابي من صاحب العمل للعامل بعد غيابه عشرين يوماً في الحالة الأولى وانقطاعه عشرة أيام في الحالة الثانية. | Read from the M/46 amending block in `boe/labor-law-ar.md`; the original text has the 2005 thresholds (20 days / 10 consecutive, warnings after 10 / 5). Annex 1's violations schedule row 15 (absence over 15 consecutive days: dismissal without award after written warning) tracks the amended article. termination-review must check the warning was issued after day 20 / day 10 and before dismissal. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic]` |
| Law Arts. 84–88 — end-of-service award and final settlement | Award of half a month's wage per year for the first five years and a full month per year thereafter, on the last wage, pro rata for parts of a year; on resignation one third after two to five consecutive years, two thirds after five to under ten, full at ten or more; commissions and variable elements may be excluded by agreement (Art. 86); full award where the worker leaves for force majeure, or a woman ends the contract within six months of marriage or three months of childbirth (Art. 87); wages and entitlements settled within one week of the end of the relationship, or two weeks where the worker ended it, the employer deducting work-related debts (Art. 88). | إذا انتهت علاقة العمل وجب على صاحب العمل أن يدفع إلى العامل مكافأة عن مدة خدمته تحسب على أساس أجر نصف شهر عن كل سنة من السنوات الخمس الأولى، وأجر شهر عن كل سنة من السنوات التالية ... إذا انتهت خدمة العامل وجب على صاحب العمل دفع أجره وتصفية حقوقه خلال أسبوع على الأكثر. | Unamended text (these articles carry no [معدلة] marker). Annex 5 cl. 11.9–11.10 restate the windows and carve out probation, resignation under two years, and Art. 80. "Wage" for the award is the total last wage (Law Art. 2 definition) unless commissions are carved out under Art. 86; whether housing and transport allowances are included is settled in favour of inclusion by the definition `[model knowledge — verify]` as to court practice on allowances paid in kind. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic]` |
| Annex 1 Arts. 58–70 (Law Arts. 66–73) — discipline | Penalties: written warning; fine (part of a day's wage up to five days' wage per month); unpaid suspension up to five days a month; withholding or deferring the increment up to a year; deferring promotion up to a year; dismissal with award for a legitimate reason; dismissal without award, notice or compensation under Law Art. 80. Penalty must be proportionate; only the penalty listed for the violation; the authorised person may substitute a lighter one; no aggravation for repetition if 180 days have passed since notification of the previous penalty; one penalty per violation; no penalty above a one-day fine without written notification of the charge, hearing the worker and recording the defence in minutes filed in the personnel file; no penalty for conduct outside work unless directly related to the work, the establishment or the manager; no disciplinary action if more than 30 days have passed since discovery without investigation, or more than 30 days since the violation was established; written notification of the penalty (registered mail or the email in the contract if refused or absent); a penalty sheet per worker; fines register and use for workers' benefit (Law Art. 73). | لا توقع المنشأة أياً من الجزاءات التي تتجاوز عقوبتها غرامة أجر يوم واحد إلا بعد إبلاغ العامل كتابة بالمخالفات المنسوبة إليه وسماع أقواله وتحقيق دفاعه، وذلك بموجب محضر يودع بملفه الخاص ... لا يجوز مساءلة العامل تأديبياً عن مخالفة مضى على كشفها أكثر من ثلاثين يوماً. | The two 30-day clocks (discovery-to-investigation, proof-to-penalty) are the most common procedural defect in KSA dismissals. internal-investigation and termination-review must date the discovery, the investigation start and the penalty decision. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Annex 1 Art. 71 (Law Art. 72, M/44) — grievance | A worker may grieve any act, procedure or penalty in writing to the establishment's competent body within 30 days (excluding official holidays) of notification, without prejudice; the establishment answers within 15 days; if rejected or unanswered in writing within 15 days, the worker may object before the labor courts within 30 days (excluding official holidays) of the rejection or of the lapse of the 15 days, whichever is earlier. | للعامل أن يتظلم من أي تصرف أو إجراء أو جزاء ... خلال ثلاثين يوماً - عدا أيام العطل الرسمية - من تاريخ إبلاغه ... كان له حق الاعتراض أمام المحاكم العمالية خلال ثلاثين يوماً - عدا أيام العطل الرسمية - من تاريخ رفض تظلمه أو انتهاء المدة المحددة للبت في التظلم أيهما أقرب. | Law Art. 72 as amended by M/44 (read from its amending block in `boe/labor-law-ar.md`) is the same 30/15/30 ladder; the original 2005 text (15-day objection to the commission) is obsolete. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Annex 1 schedule of violations and penalties | Three tables (attendance, work organisation, worker conduct) with graduated penalties for first to fourth occurrence, mostly percentages of the daily wage rising to days of wage and, for absences, to withholding of increment, deferral of promotion, dismissal with award (absence 7–10 consecutive days if total absence in the year does not exceed 30) and dismissal without award or compensation after written warning (absence over 15 consecutive days, per Law Art. 80). | أولاً: مخالفات تتعلق بمواعيد العمل ... ثانياً: مخالفات تتعلق بتنظيم العمل ... ثالثاً: مخالفات تتعلق بسلوك العامل ... الانقطاع عن العمل دون سبب مشروع مدة تزيد على خمسة عشر يوماً متصلة: الفصل دون مكافأة أو تعويض على أن يسبقه إنذار كتابي. | Only the first table (attendance) was read in full; the second and third tables were skimmed. Establishments may only impose the penalty listed against the violation (Annex 1 Art. 59) or a lighter one. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` (tables 2–3 skimmed) |
| Reg. Art. 38 (Law Art. 230) — HRSD penalties | Penalties in table 1 of the Minister's violations-and-penalties decision are imposed by administrative decision of the competent unit; table 2 penalties are sought by suit before the labor courts; inspectors submit violation reports to that unit; a centre under the Deputy Minister for Labor receives objections and settlement requests; objection to an administrative penalty decision within 60 days of notification, without suspending the fine; refunds via the Human Resources Development Fund if the objection succeeds after payment; settlement is available only after an administrative decision or final judgment and not for a violation repeated a third time in two years or settled the previous time; the settlement request is filed within 90 days of notification, decided within 90 days (enforcement may be suspended meanwhile), the violator must remove the violation, and must implement the settlement within 60 days or it lapses; a committee hears petitions against the objections centre. Law Art. 230(1) (M/46): the Ministry may impose fines and temporary closure up to half the Art. 229 maxima by decision, appealable to the administrative court; Art. 229 (M/46): fine up to SAR 100,000, closure up to 30 days, permanent closure, doubling on repetition, fines multiplied by the number of persons concerned. | يتم الاعتراض على القرار الإداري بإيقاع عقوبات مخالفات العمل خلال (ستين) يوماً من تاريخ تبليغ المخالف بالقرار الإداري، ولا يوقف هذا الاعتراض تنفيذ عقوبة الغرامة ... أن يقدم المخالف طلب التسوية خلال (تسعين) يوماً من تاريخ تبليغه ... على المخالف تنفيذ قرار تسوية المخالفة خلال (ستين) يوماً من تاريخ تبليغه به، وإلا اعتبرت التسوية ملغاة. | The schedule itself (which violation costs what, by establishment size) is a separate ministerial decision, revised per the HRSD page and per amendment-watch lead 1.5 (claimed effective 25 Feb 2026); it was not provided and its amounts are `[model knowledge — verify]`. What triggers a fine, at the level of this file: undocumented contracts, unpaid or late wages and WPS non-compliance, passport retention, Saudization and restricted-profession breaches, working non-Saudis for others, safety breaches, hours and leave breaches, and failure to keep the Art. 5 records. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` (Law Arts. 229–230: `[BOE — Arabic]`) |
| Reg. Arts. 39–40 (Law Arts. 231–232) | The violator must remove the violation within ten working days of the penalty or it counts as a repetition and the penalty is doubled; the fine is paid within 60 days of notification of the administrative decision or final judgment, failing which Ministry services are suspended until payment; a challenge before the administrative court does not suspend a table-1 fine unless that court orders suspension; fines go to the Human Resources Development Fund. | يجب على المخالف إزالة المخالفة خلال عشرة أيام عمل من تاريخ إيقاع العقوبة عليه، وفي حال عدم إزالتها خلال المدة المذكورة؛ تعتبر تكراراً للمخالفة وتضاعف العقوبة عليه ... يسدد المخالف الغرامة الموقعة عليه خلال ستون يوم من تاريخ تبليغه ... وفي حال عدم التنفيذ خلال هذه المدة؛ توقف خدمات الوزارة عنه لحين السداد. | Service suspension (Qiwa) is the practical sanction; an unpaid HRSD fine blocks visas, transfers and renewals across the whole establishment. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Reg. Arts. 32–35 (Law Arts. 161–163, 167) — minors | A minor aged 15 to under 18 may not work in mines, quarries, health-hazardous industries, arduous work, high-risk machinery, or work exposing him to moral, psychological or physical harm; no employment under 15 except the Art. 167 educational cases (with direct supervision, gradual training, no interference with schooling, no hazardous work, Ministry and licensing-body approval); night work of minors allowed only in family-only establishments, vocational schools and training centres, bakeries (except 9 pm to 4 am), and force majeure. | يحظر عمل الحدث الذي أتم الخامسة عشرة من عمره ولم يبلغ الثامنة عشرة في المهن والأعمال التي يحتمل أن تعرض صحته وسلامته وأخلاقه للخطر ... لا يجوز بأي حال من الأحوال تشغيل من لم يتم الخامسة عشرة من عمره. | hiring-review threshold rows for age. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Reg. Arts. 36–37 | Repealed ("ملغاة"). | (ملغاة) | The 2023 English Arts. 36 (nursing breaks) and 37 (social services: prayer area, meal area, disability facilities) are gone from the main body; their content survives in Annex 1 Arts. 51–52. Do not cite Reg. Arts. 36–37. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |

## Open questions for a local practitioner

- Commencement: the operative paragraphs of Ministerial Decision 115921 (publication and entry into force) were not legible in the OCR provided; the 19 February 2025 date is taken from the task brief and from the M/44 commencement date shown on the BOE portal (20/8/1446H). Confirm the decision's own commencement clause.
- Schedule of violations and penalties: the Regulations (Art. 38) operate on a separate ministerial decision. The HRSD page lists a revised schedule and the amendment-watch report claims a further revision effective 25 February 2026. Neither text was provided; every fine amount a skill needs is therefore `[model knowledge — verify]`.
- Wage Protection System: the Regulations only reference the program (Annex 1 Art. 15, Annex 5 cl. 9.1.2/11.1, Annex 4 Art. 63). The WPS decision(s) — coverage thresholds, monthly file deadline, compliance percentage, tiered service suspensions and fines, and the Mudad platform rules — were not provided.
- Resignation definition: Law Art. 2 (M/44) defines resignation by reference to a fixed-term contract, while Art. 74(3 bis) and Annex 1 Art. 57(4) list resignation as a general termination ground and Art. 75 still governs indefinite contracts. How labor courts treat a "resignation" from an indefinite contract that is submitted without 30 days' notice (Art. 79 bis clock versus Art. 75 notice and Art. 76 compensation) is unresolved on the text.
- Art. 14 Second (21) versus Law Art. 77: whether an expatriate who transfers after 12 months on 90 days' notice from a fixed-term contract owes Art. 77(2) remainder-of-term compensation, and whether contracts may waive it.
- Reg. Art. 4(1): whether an establishment under 50 workers that already adopted the model must switch to the lawyer route when it later adds any clause, and which law firms are "accredited on the Ministry's website".
- Flexible work: the penalty reference is to Ministerial Decision 178743 of 27/9/1440H "and its amendments" — not provided.
- Remote work: no article in the Regulations. The HRSD remote-work program rules, if any still apply, were not provided.
- Nitaqat: every Saudization threshold in Art. 14 depends on the Nitaqat program rules (a new phase is claimed from 26 April 2026 with the yellow band removed); the HRSD Nitaqat guide in the scratchpad was not read for this file.
- Annex 1 violations tables 2 and 3, Annex 2, Annex 3 and most of Annex 4 were skimmed, not read row by row.
- The 2023 English translation figure "27 hours per year" in Art. 22 versus the Arabic 720: confirm there is no intermediate decision that changed the annual overtime cap between 2023 and April 2025.
- Occupational fitness examinations regulation (Ministerial Decision 33232 of 11/3/1447H) and the project-management Saudization decision (70% from 14 February 2027) are listed on the HRSD page but were not read.

## How skills should use this file

- **hiring-review** loads this file at the contract-drafting and pre-documentation step and must cite: Reg. Art. 18 and Annex 5 cls. 1–4 (mandatory fields and documentation), Annex 5 cl. 5 (term; non-Saudi fixed-term only, Reg. Art. 12), cl. 6 / Reg. Art. 19 (probation 180-day cap and excluded days), cls. 9–10 (wage split), cls. 13–15 (executive-instrument clause, Portal notices, additional-terms limits), Reg. Art. 11 (restricted professions), Reg. Art. 14 (recruitment refusal grounds, note-level), Reg. Arts. 32–35 (minors), Reg. Art. 27 (part-time and flexible-work eligibility), Reg. Art. 9 and Law Art. 61(4) (non-discrimination), Annex 1 Art. 7 (seven-working-day no-show cancellation).
- **worker-classification** loads at the classification step and must cite Reg. Art. 1 (90-day conversion), Reg. Art. 27 First and Second (part-time and flexible-work definitions and caps), Reg. Art. 13 (Ajeer secondment), Reg. Art. 10 and Annex 4 (licensed labor-services suppliers).
- **wage-hour-qa** loads at the computation step and must cite Annex 5 cl. 9 (basic versus allowances), Reg. Art. 22 (720-hour cap), Reg. Art. 22 bis (compensatory leave 1.5:1, 30 days, 60-day scheduling), Reg. Art. 23 (exempt categories and their ceilings), Annex 1 Arts. 15–17 and Law Art. 90 (payment dates and bank payment), Law Art. 94 (late-wage remedy), Reg. Art. 24 (holidays). Computed overtime per Law Art. 107(1): (hourly actual wage + 0.5 × hourly basic wage) × overtime hours, which equals hourly basic wage × 1.5 × overtime hours only when the actual wage is the basic wage; hourly wage = monthly wage ÷ (monthly hours per the contract's standard); the divisor is not fixed by the Regulations and the skill must state the divisor it used and tag the result `[model knowledge — verify]` for the divisor.
- **policy-drafting** and **handbook-updates** load at the drafting step and must diff the client handbook against Annex 1 article by article, citing Reg. Arts. 3–4 (approval route and grandfathering), Annex 1 Arts. 33–44 (leave), 50–51 (maternity, nursing), 53–56 (conduct and harassment), 57 (termination grounds), 58–71 (discipline and grievance), and Reg. Art. 4(2) for clauses rendered void by the 2025 changes.
- **termination-review** loads at the grounds-and-process step and must cite Annex 1 Art. 57 / Law Art. 74 (ground), Law Art. 75 (notice 60/30), Law Art. 79 bis (resignation clock), Law Art. 80 (summary dismissal cases and warning timing), Annex 1 Arts. 63–68 (hearing, 30-day clocks, written notification), Annex 1 Art. 71 (grievance ladder), Law Arts. 84–88 and Annex 5 cls. 11.9–11.10 (award and settlement windows), Reg. Art. 22 bis(4) and Annex 5 cl. 8.2 (paid-out balances), Reg. Art. 14 Second (expatriate transfer routes). Computed end-of-service award: (years ≤ 5) × 0.5 × last monthly wage + (years > 5) × 1 × last monthly wage, pro rata for part years, then the Art. 85 fraction on resignation (1/3 for 2–5 years, 2/3 for 5–10, full at 10+), zero under two years' resignation, full under Art. 87; the skill must attach `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic]` to the formula and `[model knowledge — verify]` to any decision about which allowances are in "last wage".
- **internal-investigation** loads at the procedure step and must follow Annex 1 Arts. 53–56 (harassment committee, five-working-day windows, confidentiality, minutes) and Arts. 64–67 (hearing before penalty, 30-day clocks), using Reg. Art. 5 records as evidence sources.
- **log-leave** and **leave-tracker** load at entitlement lookup and must cite Annex 1 Arts. 33–44, Reg. Arts. 24–26, Annex 5 cl. 8 (working-day definition for annual leave), Reg. Art. 22 bis (compensatory leave balance and 60-day scheduling clock), Annex 1 Art. 50 (maternity), Reg. Art. 31 (nursing breaks, 24 months), Reg. Art. 25 (day-21 suspension of unpaid leave).
- **Stop rule:** if a skill needs a rule that is not in this table, or that is tagged `[model knowledge — verify]` (in particular any fine amount, any WPS deadline or threshold, any Nitaqat band, the remote-work rules, or the reconciliation of Art. 79 bis with Art. 75), it must say so in its output and stop or flag for Saudi counsel; it must not fill the gap from memory. Where a Law row notes that the article is marked [معدلة] in `boe/labor-law-ar.md`, the skill must cite the amended version as stated in the row, never the original text printed above the amending blocks.
# Labor dispute route: friendly settlement, labor courts, limitation and enforcement — مسار الدعوى العمالية: التسوية الودية والمحاكم العمالية والتقادم والتنفيذ

