/bin/zsh -lc "cat 'references/jurisdictions/ksa/platform-obligations.md' 'references/jurisdictions/ksa/social-insurance-law.md' 'references/jurisdictions/ksa/saudization-nitaqat.md' 'references/jurisdictions/ksa/occupational-safety.md'" in /Users/basimkhoja/Projects/Legal Consultant
 succeeded in 0ms:
# Platform obligations (Qiwa, Mudad/WPS, Musaned, Absher/Muqeem, GOSI online) — الالتزامات النظامية عبر المنصات (قوى، مدد، مساند، أبشر/مقيم، التأمينات)

<!-- Written 2026-09-04. This is not one instrument: it maps where the platforms carry a legal duty for a corporate employer rather than a convenience. Primary texts read: Labor Law (Arabic, laws.boe.gov.sa) Arts. 15, 16, 32-40, 51-53, 90, 231-235, 239; HRSD Implementing Regulation of the Labor Law (April 2025 consolidated PDF, Arabic) Arts. 12, 13, 14, 18, 19, the flexible-work rules, the model work-organisation regulation Art. 15, and the labour-services licensing rules; Social Insurance Law (Arabic) Arts. 7-10. Platform terms of use, WPS ministerial decisions, and Absher/Muqeem rules were NOT in the source set. -->

## Instrument

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Jurisdiction | `ksa` |
| Instrument | Employer duties performed through government platforms: Qiwa (قوى, HRSD: establishment file, contract documentation, work permits, visas, transfer of services, Nitaqat); Mudad (مدد, HRSD/SAMA: Wage Protection System wage files and payroll); Musaned (مساند, HRSD: domestic-worker recruitment and contracts; noted only); Absher and Muqeem (أبشر / مقيم, Ministry of Interior: iqama, exit/re-entry and final-exit visas); GOSI online services (التأمينات الاجتماعية: registration, wage declarations, contributions). Statutory sources: Labor Law Arts. 15-16, 32-40, 51-53, 90 and the penalties chapter; Implementing Regulation Arts. 12-14, 18-19; Social Insurance Law Arts. 7-10 |
| Issuing instrument | Labor Law: Royal Decree No. M/51 of 23/8/1426H, most recently amended by Royal Decree M/44 of 8/2/1446H (12 August 2024). Implementing Regulation of the Labor Law and its annexes: HRSD Ministerial Decision No. 115921 of 19/8/1446H (18 February 2025; the decision PDF is a scan and was not read; the regulation text was read from HRSD's April 2025 consolidated PDF). Social Insurance Law: Royal Decree No. M/273 of 26/12/1445H. The WPS ministerial decisions, the Qiwa contract-authentication decisions, and the labour-mobility (transfer without consent) decision of 2021 are known only by reputation and are tagged model knowledge |
| Issuing authority | HRSD (Qiwa, Mudad, Musaned, Ajeer); Ministry of Interior (Absher, Muqeem); GOSI |
| Effective date | Labor Law 2006-04-26; the M/44 of 1446H amendments took effect on 20/8/1446H (19 February 2025) per the portal's note on each amended article ("ويعمل بها من تاريخ 1446/8/20هـ"); the M/46 of 1436H amendments (penalties chapter, Arts. 35, 52-55, 74, 90) date from 2015; Implementing Regulation April 2025 (adoption February 2025); Social Insurance Law 2024-07-03. Platform go-live dates (Qiwa 2019-2020, Mudad WPS 2020-2021, labour-mobility rules 14 March 2021) are `[model knowledge — verify]` |
| Amendment history | Labor Law: the portal marks 106 articles as amended. Of the articles relied on below: Arts. 15, 16, 32, 33, 34, 36 and 38 are unamended; Art. 30 replaced by M/44 of 1446H (adds the licensed "outsourcing activity"); Art. 35 replaced by M/46 of 1436H and again by M/44; Art. 37 replaced by M/44 (one-year default term); Art. 39 replaced by M/24 of 1434H and again by M/44 (single paragraph, ministry inspection and Ministry of Interior referral); Art. 40(1) reworded by M/44 ("delay fines caused by the employer"); Art. 51 amended by M/44 (documentation duty); Art. 52 replaced by M/46 and para (1) reworded by M/44 (template per contract type, basic rights and obligations); Art. 53 amended by M/46 and M/44 (probation up to 180 days total); Art. 74 amended by M/46, M/134 of 1440H (retirement age per the Social Insurance Law) and M/44 (resignation, bankruptcy-court termination); Art. 90 replaced by M/46 (bank payment mandatory); penalties chapter restructured by M/46 into Arts. 229-233, with Art. 229 bis added and Art. 230(5) amended by M/44. Rows citing these articles were read from the "تعديلات المادة" (wording in force) blocks of the regenerated source file; the HRSD Implementing Regulation (April 2025) quotes the same in-force wording for Arts. 51-53. Amendment-watch leads of 2026-09-04: wage-clause direct enforcement extended to open-ended contracts from 6 August 2026 (lead 1.1); Qiwa-documentation condition for Saudization credit from 15 April 2026 and a revised penalties schedule from 25 February 2026 (lead 1.5); none confirmed |
| Official source (authoritative language) | Labor Law: https://laws.boe.gov.sa/BoeLaws/Laws/LawDetails/08381293-6388-48e2-8ad2-a9a700f2aa94/1 . Implementing Regulation: https://www.hrsd.gov.sa/sites/default/files/2025-04/اللائحة التنفيذية لنظام العمل وملحقاتها.pdf . Social Insurance Law: https://laws.boe.gov.sa/BoeLaws/Laws/LawDetails/eaee8a20-3a54-4aaf-b0d9-b1ad00998962/1 . Platforms: qiwa.sa, mudad.com.sa, musaned.com.sa, absher.sa, muqeem.sa, gosi.gov.sa (terms not read) |
